2058. Find the Minimum and Maximum Number of Nodes Between Critical Points
Problem Description
A critical point in a linked list is defined as either a local maxima or a local minima.
 * A node is a local maxima if its value is strictly greater than the previous and next nodes.
 * A node is a local minima if its value is strictly smaller than the previous and next nodes.
Given a linked list head, return an array [minDistance, maxDistance]. If there are fewer than two critical points, return [-1, -1].
Pattern & Intuition
 * Pattern: Fixed-Size Sliding Window (Triplet Traversal) + Single-Pass Greedy Tracking.
 * Triplet Window: Traverse using three nodes (prev, curr, curr.next) to identify whether curr is a peak or valley.
 * Min Distance: Always occurs between two adjacent critical points. Track the previous critical point index to compute min(min_dist, curr_idx - prev_idx).
 * Max Distance: Always spans the first and the last critical point (last_idx - first_idx).
Implementation (Python 3)
# Definition for singly-linked list.
# class ListNode:
#     def __init__(self, val=0, next=None):
#         self.val = val
#         self.next = next

class Solution:
    def nodesBetweenCriticalPoints(self, head: Optional[ListNode]) -> List[int]:
        if not head or not head.next or not head.next.next:
            return [-1, -1]
        
        first_cp = -1
        prev_cp = -1
        min_dist = float('inf')
        
        prev = head
        curr = head.next
        idx = 1
        
        while curr.next:
            # Check if current node is a local maxima or minima
            is_critical = (curr.val > prev.val and curr.val > curr.next.val) or \
                          (curr.val < prev.val and curr.val < curr.next.val)
            
            if is_critical:
                if first_cp == -1:
                    first_cp = idx
                else:
                    min_dist = min(min_dist, idx - prev_cp)
                prev_cp = idx
            
            prev = curr
            curr = curr.next
            idx += 1
            
        # If fewer than 2 critical points were found
        if first_cp == -1 or prev_cp == first_cp:
            return [-1, -1]
        
        max_dist = prev_cp - first_cp
        return [min_dist, max_dist]

Complexity Analysis
| Metric | Complexity | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Time Complexity | O(N) | Single traversal over the linked list of N nodes. |
| Space Complexity | O(1) | Uses a fixed number of pointer and index variables without extra memory. |
